Explanation of 4.1 3.-4.
  3. updating queues
  - service counter is a timer for the customer currently being served by cashier
  - service counter is decremented each second before rest of logic is executed
  - if the service counter is 0 then the cashier is available and the next customer is served
  - wait time is calculated by the time the customer leaves the queue-customers arrival time
    *if customers are unsorted simulation will still run but wait times will be very large
  - service counter is set to service time of next customer+some random amount 
    based on maximum random time set in configurations menu (section 3)
  - lane queue time is updated
  - if queues are of very different length some customers may move to end of other queues
    *not sure if this part is needed
  4. adding to queues
  - if time<=next arrival time, customer moved to lanes
  - placement depends on the number of items the customer has and the lane queue time
  - possible situations
    - customer does not count as priority, cashier is available and queue is empty->customer skips queue
    - priority cashier is available, queue is empty-> customer skips queue regardless of # items
  - otherwise customer must choose lane based on equation
    - lane length=total items in queue*some amount for priority queues
      *subject to change
    - customers choose lane based on smallest lane length (can't see customer being served for now)
    - customers that do not qualify for priority queues may enter priority queues 
      if there is a significant difference in length
    - customers that qualify for priority queues may enter any lane
  - once customer is added to queue, lane queue time is updated
  - section is contained in while loop so any number of customers can be moved to lanes
    if they arrive at the same time
    







